A||N||4||Dan86gt3.8||are 86 GT "fastback" windows held on by tape or a bolt?||||1||
Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||06-15-2000||12:21 PM||||Yes I got some differing opinnions on this.  I believe they are called the sail panels, but they are thoose crapy little windows that they put in the fastback.  Mine are cracked and stuff anywyas so I guess its not a big deal if the break even more.  I thoiught I had heard someone say it was tape before but I was not sure.  thanks in advance for any info you have!||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||06-15-2000||01:04 PM||||one of my quater windows broke when broom hit it... they have this sticky yellow backing on them (tape?).  the ones from the fiero store come with tape to hold them on so i'm assuming that the originals do too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||06-15-2000||02:51 PM||||Yep they're just held on by tape.  If they're already all cracked and you don't care about them, the easiest way to get 'em off is to break 'em off...||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||06-15-2000||03:55 PM||||Not just any tape.  I think 3M makes a good heavy duty double-sided tape.||||reg||3
Z||000004||CJ||06-16-2000||11:34 PM||||According to the 1988 shop manual, the fastback "windows" your talking about are held on with double back tape.  To remove them, go to the front edge of the window and you can dig out a string in the space.  As you pull the string out, it cuts the tape.  Don't have the shop manual in front of me, but I read this description a few weeks ago when I was browsing.||||reg||1
